spice-html5, vendored for Rackoon's SPICE console
==================================================

Upstream:  https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/spice/spice-html5
Commit:    b372aab6e5ab3ce056f486d3bdcd3845f9e34aad (2026-09-21, "Remove the ES module polyfill")
License:   LGPL-3.0-or-later (COPYING.LESSER, with the GPL text in COPYING);
           thirdparty/ keeps its own (BSD/MIT style) notices.

The files are the upstream src/ directory unchanged, except for the changes
marked "RACKOON PATCH" and one added file:

1. spiceconn.js: `new WebSocket(uri, 'binary')` became `createSocket(uri, 'binary')`
   (rackoon-socket.js). Rackoon registers a factory for the session URL so each
   SPICE channel (main, display, inputs, cursor, ...) becomes one channel of the
   multiplexed console WebSocket (CONTRACT.md 4). Unknown URLs still get a real
   WebSocket.
2. display.js: the primary canvas is no longer focused automatically and the
   host clipboard is not offered on first render. Keys are captured only after
   the user clicks the screen (REMOTE-CONSOLE.md 10).
3. main.js: clipboard sharing with the guest agent is off unless
   `clipboard_sharing === true` on the main connection (Rackoon never sets it):
   the browser clipboard is never read without a user gesture and guest-to-host
   clipboard is opt-in (REMOTE-CONSOLE.md 6.7).
4. display.js (bug fix, worth sending upstream): when the guest resets or
   switches video modes, SURFACE_CREATE for the same surface id ran before the
   queued SURFACE_DESTROY, which was then skipped; the stale canvas stayed on
   top of the new one (frozen or black screen after a reboot). A surface that
   is being replaced is now removed at once.
5. rackoon-socket.js (added): the socket factory registry.
6. main.d.ts, rackoon-socket.d.ts (added): TypeScript declarations for the parts
   Rackoon calls.

To update: copy upstream src/ over this directory, re-apply 1-4 (grep for
RACKOON PATCH in the old copy) and test a SPICE console end to end.
